# VS Code snippet files are JSONC by convention, but this one is kept as strict
# JSON so `JSON.parse` tooling (see docs/content/docs/fork/vscode-snippets.md)
# works. Prettier rewrites it with trailing commas, which breaks that.
.vscode/*.code-snippets

# Generated by scripts/build-skill.mjs. Prettier reflows the tables and code
# fences, which makes `node scripts/build-skill.mjs --check` fail on a clean
# tree. Edit the sources instead: layouts/_shortcodes/, .vscode/hextra.code-snippets,
# data/icons.yaml.
skills/hextra/references/shortcodes.md
skills/hextra/references/icons.md

# Version-stamped by scripts/build-skill.mjs from the root VERSION file, and
# serialized with JSON.stringify. Prettier reflows the arrays, which would make
# `node scripts/build-skill.mjs --check` fail on a clean tree. Edit any field
# except "version" by hand; the generator preserves it.
.claude-plugin/plugin.json
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json

# A CSS file whose Hugo template code lives inside a CSS comment, so Hugo can
# derive the variables at build time. Prettier's CSS parser crashes on the
# template actions, and renaming it so the go-template parser picks it up makes
# things worse: that parser reflows the comment and drops the :root block. There
# is no extension or edit that makes this file safe to format.
assets/css/variables.css

# A Hugo template that emits the FlexSearch index, so it opens with a template
# action and is not valid JSON. Renaming it so prettier skips it is not an
# option either: Hugo derives the media type from the extension, and a non-.json
# source leaves the generated file with no mimetype, which fails minification.
assets/json/search-data.json
